mod:variadic_tail_view;
// A VARIADIC TAIL IS STORAGE BUILT FOR THE CALL, SO THE SLOT ITSELF IS A BORROW OF THIS FRAME (DEF-519, HIGH by kind, landing 177d2b). `pass vs` handed the caller a view it couldn't
// have a chain for, the tail's arguments carrying nothing, and once the caller had returned the view read what the stack held next (`u1_whole`, 83 at -O0 and 60 at -O2 on main, no `=>!`, no lock).
// So whatever hands the tail itself on is BORROW-001, as `@vs[0i64]` always was: `u*` is each road, whole, ranged, a local copy, a holder, a helper, a forwarding spread, a store through a parameter.
// An element read out of it is the argument and stays on the summary's PASS bit, in `variadic_tail_view_ok.npk` and `for_pick_binding_source_ok.npk`.
// THE PRICE, `c*`, RIGHT PROGRAMS NOW REFUSED, none in the tree or the libraries: the callee can't tell a caller that keeps the view in its own frame from one that returns it, so `g` itself is
// refused whoever calls it. The road is to copy what you need out of the tail.
